00:09:33.070 --> 00:09:34.740
- All right, so let's get into this.

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:35.960
In this episode,

00:09:35.960 --> 00:09:37.607
we're talking about some of the things

00:09:37.607 --> 00:09:42.290
that people can do to create
and mimic in their lives

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:45.090
the biological adversity

00:09:45.090 --> 00:09:48.580
that's more conducive

00:09:48.580 --> 00:09:51.009
to better lifespans and
health spans that we call-

00:09:51.009 --> 00:09:52.820
- We call these adversity mimetics.

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:53.995
- We call these that.

00:09:53.995 --> 00:09:54.893
I mean, when you say we call these that,

00:09:54.893 --> 00:09:56.700
is it like you and I call them that?

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:58.300
'Cause I know we call them
that, but is it like...

00:09:58.300 --> 00:09:59.740
Is that a term that scientists use,

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:00.573
that people actually use right now?

00:10:00.573 --> 00:10:01.610
- No, we just made it up.

00:10:01.610 --> 00:10:02.970
- You're just making it up.

00:10:02.970 --> 00:10:04.350
But it's a good word, right?

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:06.174
- We'll use it, trademark.

00:10:06.174 --> 00:10:08.460
- And the reason why
adversity is important

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:12.220
ties back to this idea
that you've proposed

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:14.380
of a survival circuit.

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:15.620
So before we move forward into this,

00:10:15.620 --> 00:10:18.050
let's talk about the survival circuit.

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:20.950
We don't have to go way,
way back in history.

00:10:20.950 --> 00:10:22.160
- Not 4 Billion years,

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:23.510
we'll come forward in time a little bit?

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:25.670
- Yeah, you can go back 4 billion years,

00:10:25.670 --> 00:10:27.500
and that's in the book.

00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:29.620
But we're going to start in the 1990s

00:10:29.620 --> 00:10:33.840
with Cynthia Kenyon and
